   "added REQ_HOLE_CENTRES_WIDTH: the brief puts the holes' centres on a rectangle 36 mm along that side, and nothing in the record carried it.",
   "added REQ_HOLES_4MM: the brief states 4 open holes of 4 mm, counted on the built part by diameter. A claim bound to a hole's parameter passes whenever some hole reads that parameter -- a collar had both set screws drawn at the bore's 12 mm, and no bore, and it passed.",
   "added REQ_PART_LONG: the brief says the part is 70 mm long, and nothing measured that on the part itself -- a parameter reads back what the design declares, on a part of any size.",
   "added REQ_PART_WIDE: the brief says the part is 50 mm wide, and nothing measured that on the part itself -- a parameter reads back what the design declares, on a part of any size.",
   "added REQ_PART_THICK: the brief says the part is 4 mm thick, and nothing measured that on the part itself -- a parameter reads back what the design declares, on a part of any size.",
   "REQ_PART_LONG, REQ_PART_WIDE, REQ_PART_THICK measured on the part laid flat: the brief bends it, and a bent part's sizes are its sizes along the plate -- a sheet keeps its length along its middle when it is bent.",
